 # OpenVDB DDA
 
-Also called: VDB DDA, Digital Differential Analyzer specialized for OpenVDB grids, Digital Differential Analyzer for OpenVDB
+Also called: Digital Differential Analyzer for OpenVDB, Digital Differential Analyzer specialized for OpenVDB grids, PointTreeMarcher, VDB DDA
 
 ## Overview
-OpenVDB DDA is a Digital Differential Analyzer traversal algorithm specialized for OpenVDB grids, conceptually similar to Bresenham's line algorithm applied to a 3D ray intersecting OpenVDB nodes or voxels [S2, S5, unofficial][S6]. It iterates through grid elements (voxels or tree nodes) intersected by a ray, using a fixed step-size defined by the template parameter `Log2Dim` [S1][S5, unofficial]. Unlike Hierarchical DDA (HDDA) which uses variable step-sizes to skip empty space, OpenVDB DDA marches through every node or voxel boundary along the ray path [S1]. It serves as the foundational traversal kernel for higher-level hierarchical methods like `LevelSetHDDA` and `VolumeHDDA`, which wrap this DDA to handle tree structures and empty space skipping [S2, S4, unofficial].
+OpenVDB DDA is a Digital Differential Analyzer traversal algorithm specialized for OpenVDB grids, conceptually similar to Bresenham's line algorithm applied to a 3D ray intersecting OpenVDB nodes or voxels [S2, S5, unofficial][S6]. It iterates through grid elements intersected by a ray using a fixed step-size defined by the template parameter `Log2Dim` [S1][S5, unofficial]. Unlike Hierarchical DDA (HDDA) which uses variable step-sizes to skip empty space, OpenVDB DDA marches through every node or voxel boundary along the ray path [S1].
 
